              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 3295,
                "end_index": 3435,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "When the warm \"healthy\" red tones disappear, our visual system exaggerates the contrast, making us perceive the person as starkly \"greenish\""
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                14
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 3438,
                "end_index": 3646,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "#### Historical Context: Chlorosis (The \"Green Sickness\")\nHistorically, there was a very real medical condition known as **chlorosis**, or \"green sickness,\" which was widespread in the 18th and 19th centuries"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                14
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 3648,
                "end_index": 3697,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "It primarily affected young, undernourished women"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                14
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 3699,
                "end_index": 3795,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Today, we know chlorosis was actually severe **hypochromic anemia** (a profound iron deficiency)"
